 "title": "The knot sphere contains Sperner's lemma",
 "subject": "Whether the knot sphere's Euler count reduces to, or from, a planar principle with known proof-complexity bounds",
 "conclusion": "One-sided 2D Sperner reduces to finding a violated line of the knot sphere by depth-2 decision trees, the violated lines falling exactly in the boundary-oriented full triangles, with the six corners as Sperner's boundary. So query and resolution-width bounds for grid Sperner transfer, and the sphere's width question becomes Sperner's, reduced to an open winding-control lemma.",
